# Balloon‑Scape

**Balloon‑Scape** is a 2D top-down open-world adventure game built entirely in GameMaker Studio.  
Developed independently at age 15, this project demonstrates complex system design, state management, AI programming, and scalable game architecture.

You can play Balloon-Scape here: https://jordanfeinstein.itch.io/balloon-scape

---

## Project Overview

Balloon‑Scape lets players explore a dynamic world, interact with NPCs, fight enemies, and complete objectives.  
Inspired by classic top-down games like Zelda, it emphasizes:

- Multi-directional movement and player actions (walking, shooting, swimming, interacting)  
- Complex enemy AI with multiple states (wandering, chasing, shooting)  
- Performance-conscious world design using distance-based object activation  
- Modular player and enemy state machines for scalable game logic 
-Complex interaction between assets

With **over 4,700 lines of code**, all art assets created in GameMaker Studio, and integrated sound effects, this project highlights independent development and algorithmic thinking.

---

## Technical Highlights

- **Language:** GameMaker Language (GML)  
- **Engine:** GameMaker Studio  
- **Core Systems:**  
  - Player and enemy state machines  
  - AI with multiple behaviors and projectile attacks  
  - Inventory system using custom data structures  
  - Cutscenes and pause system with RAM-based screenshot overlay  
  - Distance-based object activation/deactivation for performance  
- **Assets:** Custom sprites and animations; free online sound effects  
- **Version Control:** Git + GitHub (uploaded recently; development history is local)

---

## Gameplay

- Move with arrow keys (configurable)  
- Interact with objects and NPCs  
- Fight enemies using shooting powers  
- Collect items and manage inventory  
- Explore the open world, engage in cutscenes, and complete objectives

---

## Skills Demonstrated

- Independent project development from scratch  
- System design for scalable, complex game mechanics  
- Algorithmic thinking for AI and performance optimization  
- Creative problem-solving in state management, UI, and inventory systems  
- Self-taught programming and asset creation  

This project illustrates the ability to design, implement, and optimize a large-scale software system independently.  

